  "group": "legacy",
  "title": "legacy, memory, through, relaxed",
  "summary": "A byte-bounded exact LRU inside the application process. Included in the budget rather than treated as free. Write-through: the new value is never published before the database commit; the writer tombstones, commits, then republishes only the committed representation. A reader may receive an older committed value than the latest acknowledged write, and every such read is counted. The legacy model supplies no token, so strict freshness rests on invalidation alone or on an authoritative read.",
  "risk": "may return stale committed data; throughput is only reportable with the wrong-read count and rate beside it",
